rent's acceptance requires these tickets to be filed and linked. Filed in the 2026-11-04 gap pass (WS-F) so the design work exists and can be prioritised on its own merits; implementation timing is a separate decision, possibly months out.\n\n## What this design must settle\n\nHuman-readable export, hand-authored upload UX, and agent-authored KDL statements (§1.4 of the parent): one validation + decomposition pipeline, three front doors.\n\n## Context from the parent\n\nThe parent design fixes KDL as the human presentation format over ID data, decomposition into atomic triples, and ANSI SQL/PGQ querying. The parent issue carries the surrounding decisions this ticket must not re-decide; where this ticket's answer would change a parent decision, record that explicitly rather than silently forking it.\n\n## Decision record expected\n\nClose this design with a recorded decision (on this issue or in a `doc/` record linked from it): the chosen shape, the alternatives rejected and why, and the invariants implementation must hold. If the design splits further, file the splits and link them here rather than growing this issue.\n\n## Relations\n\nParent: #5688. Programme: epic #2056. Filed by WS-F (2026-11-04 ID design gap & expansion pass).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A design note settles the KDL presentation surfaces of §1.4 of #5688: human-readable export, hand-authored upload UX, and agent-authored KDL statements.\n- The design shows all three surfaces sharing one validation + decomposition pipeline, and names where any surface-specific step lives and why.\n- Round-trip expectations for exported-then-reimported KDL are stated (or explicitly deferred with a named follow-on).\n","closed_by":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","follower